From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: media: cedrus: an H.265 reference must be a picture decoded here

A reference list entry is an index into the job's DPB, and the engine
takes it as a frame-info slot. In damaged streams the job can hand in
0xff (GStreamer's value for a reference it does not have, by all
appearances): the driver wrote it unchecked into the list word - the
long-term bit and 0x7f, far outside the 17 slots it fills - and read
dpb[0xff] itself for the long-term flag and the low-delay test. And an
entry can name a picture that exists as a buffer but was never decoded
here, or whose decode was refused before its MV column buffer existed:
its slot then carries address 0 for the MV columns, the engine reads
IOVA 0 and does not come back from it (the watchdog ends the job).

Measured on the HY310, 14.10.2026 (a logging copy of this driver,
damaged hevc8/hevc10 sets): of about 24 500 P and B
jobs two had an entry outside the DPB, both 0xff in L0, and both read
from an unmapped address and never finished. The reads at IOVA 0 and the
watchdog timeouts behind them (five in one run next to an AV1 stream)
were gone once the reference's MV column buffer was required. No other
job had either; valid streams never do.

Such a job is refused with -EINVAL before the engine is touched, after the
capture buffer's MV column buffer exists, so a refused job leaves no picture
without one. (Written after 0277 as it stood then, which refused invalid H.264
indices; since 23.10.2026 0277 is the upstream fix that skips them, and
upstream prefers skipping for H.265 too - TODO 2.146 before 0309 goes upstream.)
---
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h265.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_h265.c
@@ -413,6 +413,44 @@
 	}
 }
 
+/*
+ * A reference list entry is an index into the DPB the job hands in. The
+ * engine takes it as a frame-info slot; past num_active_dpb_entries there
+ * is no picture, and 0xff - what userspace sends for a reference it does
+ * not have - becomes slot 0x7f with the long-term bit, far outside the 17
+ * slots the driver writes. The driver itself reads dpb[] with it as well.
+ */
+static int cedrus_h265_check_ref_list(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx,
+				      const u8 list[], unsigned int num,
+				      const struct v4l2_hevc_dpb_entry *dpb,
+				      u8 num_active_dpb_entries)
+{
+	struct vb2_queue *vq = v4l2_m2m_get_vq(ctx->fh.m2m_ctx,
+					       V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE);
+	unsigned int i;
+
+	if (num > V4L2_HEVC_DPB_ENTRIES_NUM_MAX)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < num; i++) {
+		struct vb2_buffer *buf;
+
+		if (list[i] >= num_active_dpb_entries)
+			return -EINVAL;
+		/*
+		 * The picture must exist and have been decoded here: its MV
+		 * column buffer comes with its first decode, and without it
+		 * the slot would carry address 0 - the engine then reads IOVA
+		 * 0 and does not come back from it (watchdog).
+		 */
+		buf = vb2_find_buffer(vq, dpb[list[i]].timestamp);
+		if (!buf || !vb2_to_cedrus_buffer(buf)->codec.h265.mv_col_buf_size)
+			return -EINVAL;
+	}
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static int cedrus_h265_setup(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx, struct cedrus_run *run)
 {
 	struct cedrus_dev *dev = ctx->dev;
@@ -483,6 +521,24 @@
 		}
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * After the MV column buffer of this capture buffer exists, so that a
+	 * rejected job does not leave a picture without one behind.
+	 */
+	if (slice_params->slice_type != V4L2_HEVC_SLICE_TYPE_I &&
+	    cedrus_h265_check_ref_list(ctx, slice_params->ref_idx_l0,
+				       slice_params->num_ref_idx_l0_active_minus1 + 1,
+				       decode_params->dpb,
+				       decode_params->num_active_dpb_entries))
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	if (slice_params->slice_type == V4L2_HEVC_SLICE_TYPE_B &&
+	    cedrus_h265_check_ref_list(ctx, slice_params->ref_idx_l1,
+				       slice_params->num_ref_idx_l1_active_minus1 + 1,
+				       decode_params->dpb,
+				       decode_params->num_active_dpb_entries))
+		return -EINVAL;
+
 	/* Activate H265 engine. */
 	cedrus_engine_enable(ctx);
 
